{"type":"text","timestamp":1790409005478,"sessionID":"ses_f235718cfffemZJcgMDNaJ2EQY","part":{"id":"prt_0dcb1598f001rwhmDd3HGb9Q6W","messageID":"msg_0dcb105c7001AMfuha3aSbXuKZ","sessionID":"ses_f235718cfffemZJcgMDNaJ2EQY","type":"text","text":"Done. The muzzle flash effect prefab is complete. Here's what the scene contains:\n\n- **Root `Node3D`** with `generic_effect_handler.gd` script, `optional_light_path` pointing at the `MuzzleFlash` OmniLight child\n- **`MuzzleFlash`** OmniLight3D — energy 4.0, range 6.0, warm amber color, fades over 0.2s via the handler script\n- **`SmokeParticles`** GPUParticles3D — 16 particles, zero gravity, upward direction with 40° spread, `StandardMaterial3D` with transparent billboard mode (3 = `BILLBOARD_ENABLED`) and a radial `GradientTexture2D` for volumetric smoke puffs\n- **`MuzzleFireLeft`** / **`MuzzleFireRight`** — two opposing one-shot GPUParticles3D systems (1 particle each, 0.15s lifetime), each with the `muzzle_flash.gdshader` `ShaderMaterial` and a 3×3 `QuadMesh` draw pass for dual-sided rendering\n\n`scenes/main.tscn` already referenced the effect scene — no changes needed there. The scene runs cleanly in Godot 4.4.1 headless mode.","time":{"start":1790409005455,"end":1790409005458},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_361e6bac-d553-4cca-bf47-f41bbd3769af"}}}}
